{
  "id": "novation-launchpad-mini",
  "name": "Novation Launchpad Mini",
  "match": {"card_ids": ["Mini"], "card_names": ["Launchpad Mini"], "usb_ids": ["1235:0036"]},
  "description": "An 8 by 8 pad grid, eight round buttons along the top and eight down the right side, in the power-on X-Y layout. The grid is read in rows: each bank of the panel is a pair of rows, six pads and six, bank A on rows 1 and 2, bank B on rows 3 and 4, bank C on rows 5 and 6, each in its own colour. Beside the banks, two pads wide: the presets of the shader on screen. Row 7: shaders and Vibes on the left, the effect on the right. Row 8: the clip's transport on the left, the shader's first four controls as presses on the right. The round buttons on the right: A to D are Room scenes, E to H are the screen itself in the panel's order (Fade, Freeze, Stop, Blackout). The top row holds what is used least.",
  "note": "From Novation's Launchpad S Programmer's Reference (the X-Y layout figure and the message examples), which the original Launchpad Mini shares, and one recording of the owner's Launchpad Mini on the box (notes 20 to 103 and CC 104 to 111: every one fits the X-Y layout, and note 20 does not exist in the other, drum rack, layout). The recording did not cover every pad. Not yet confirmed by pressing every control.",
  "sources": ["Novation Launchpad S Programmer's Reference Manual, version 1.02: X-Y layout (key = 16 x row + column), top row controllers 68h to 6Fh (104 to 111)", "A recording of the owner's Launchpad Mini on the test Pi, 2026-09-30 (project-log/DECISIONS.md D21): notes 20 to 103, CC 104 to 111"],
